13#issuecomment-3367749661","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110613","id":3367749661,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7Iu8gd","user":{"login":"bubba2k","id":64813843,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY0ODEzODQz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/64813843?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bubba2k","html_url":"https://github.com/bubba2k","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bubba2k/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bubba2k/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bubba2k/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bubba2k/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bubba2k/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bubba2k/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bubba2k/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bubba2k/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bubba2k/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-04T01:45:57Z","updated_at":"2025-10-04T01:46:28Z","body":"If I may chime in, passing a NaN is probably more of a user error, but IME audio effect units tend to have a somewhat specific (and often unintuitive) range of parameter values they are well defined for.\nIn the code these ranges seem to already be defined for pretty much all effect parameters with the `PROPERTY_HINT_RANGE` hint, and enforced in the UI. \nSo IMO it would be quite reasonable to check for these ranges and warn and maybe clamp inside setters as well. This would also cover NaNs.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3367749661/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]